    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0374" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg276"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum handed to the Secretary by Minister
                        Wu.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of a cablegram sent by
                        Viceroy Liu Kun-Yih and Viceroy Chang Chih-Tung, dated at Nankin July 3,
                        1900, and received by Minister Wu Ting-fang the same day.</hi></p>
                <p>Please inform Secretary of State that, it being feared that if military
                    operations shall be pressed more forcibly in northern China the people in
                    eastern and southern China may become agitated, a clear understanding should be
                    arrived at; that regardless of what may happen (in <pb facs="0375" n="277"
                        xml:id="pg277"/> the north), the foreign powers agree not to dispatch forces
                    to the Yangtze Valley or the interior of Kiangsu and Chekiang provinces, and the
                    undersigned also agree to guarantee protection in accordance with the treaties
                    to the lives and properties of people of all nationalities within their
                    respective jurisdictions.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Liu Kun-Yih</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chang Chih-Tung</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
